<figure id="alg4" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 4</span> </span> BD Decomposition (Row)</figcaption>
<div id="alg4.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg4.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
          
          
         <math id="alg4.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}\leftarrow\vec{U}\vec{V}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}\leftarrow\vec{U}\vec{V}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg4.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> with rank <math id="alg4.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
          
          
         Extract first-<math id="alg4.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> rows: <math id="alg4.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}_{F}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}_{F}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> first <math id="alg4.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> rows of <math id="alg4.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
          
          
         Extract last-<math id="alg4.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> rows: <math id="alg4.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}_{L}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}_{L}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> last <math id="alg4.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> rows of <math id="alg4.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
          
          
         Solve coefficients:<math id="alg4.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}_{F}\leftarrow\mathrm{linsolve}(\mathbf{W}^{\prime}\setminus\mathbf{B}_{F}=\mathbf{C}_{F}\mathbf{B}_{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>linsolve</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}_{F}\leftarrow\mathrm{linsolve}(\mathbf{W}^{\prime}\setminus\mathbf{B}_{F}=\mathbf{C}_{F}\mathbf{B}_{F})</annotation></semantics></math><math id="alg4.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}_{L}\leftarrow\mathrm{linsolve}(\mathbf{W}^{\prime}\setminus\mathbf{B}_{L}=\mathbf{C}_{L}\mathbf{B}_{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>linsolve</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}_{L}\leftarrow\mathrm{linsolve}(\mathbf{W}^{\prime}\setminus\mathbf{B}_{L}=\mathbf{C}_{L}\mathbf{B}_{L})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
          
          
         Compute residuals<math id="alg4.l4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{F}\leftarrow\bigl\lVert\mathbf{W}-\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{B}_{F}\\
\mathbf{C}_{F}\mathbf{B}_{F}\end{bmatrix}\bigr\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{F}\leftarrow\bigl\lVert\mathbf{W}-\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{B}_{F}\\
\mathbf{C}_{F}\mathbf{B}_{F}\end{bmatrix}\bigr\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math><math id="alg4.l4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{L}\leftarrow\bigl\lVert\mathbf{W}-\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{C}_{L}\mathbf{B}_{L}\\
\mathbf{B}_{L}\end{bmatrix}\bigr\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{L}\leftarrow\bigl\lVert\mathbf{W}-\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{C}_{L}\mathbf{B}_{L}\\
\mathbf{B}_{L}\end{bmatrix}\bigr\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
          
          
         <span id="alg4.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Select better candidateif</span> <math id="alg4.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{F}\leq R_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{F}\leq R_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <span id="alg4.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">tag<math id="alg4.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span> FIRST, <math id="alg4.l5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}\leftarrow\mathbf{B}_{\text{F}},\;\mathbf{C}\leftarrow\mathbf{C}_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mtext>F</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}\leftarrow\mathbf{B}_{\text{F}},\;\mathbf{C}\leftarrow\mathbf{C}_{F}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg4.l5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span> <span id="alg4.l5.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">tag<math id="alg4.l5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span> LAST, <math id="alg4.l5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}\leftarrow\mathbf{B}_{L},\;\mathbf{C}\leftarrow\mathbf{C}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}\leftarrow\mathbf{B}_{L},\;\mathbf{C}\leftarrow\mathbf{C}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l5a" class="ltx_listingline">
          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
          
          
         <span id="alg4.l5a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">tag</span>, basis matrix <math id="alg4.l5a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, coefficient matrix <math id="alg4.l5a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐂</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg5" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 5</span> </span> BD Reconstruction (Row)</figcaption>
<div id="alg5.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg5.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
          
          
         <span id="alg5.l0.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">tag</span>, basis matrix <math id="alg5.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, coefficient matrix <math id="alg5.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}\in\mathbb{R}^{(m-r)\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}\in\mathbb{R}^{(m-r)\times r}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg5.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
          
          
         <span id="alg5.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <span id="alg5.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">tag</span> <math id="alg5.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=</annotation></semantics></math> FIRST <span id="alg5.l1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
{type (1) in Equation <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.2 Selection of Basis ‣ 3 Method ‣ Accelerating Attention with Basis Decomposition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>}

<table id="A0.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}\;\leftarrow\;\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{B}\\
\mathbf{C}\,\mathbf{B}\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>𝐁</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}\;\leftarrow\;\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{B}\\
\mathbf{C}\,\mathbf{B}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg5.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
          
          
         <span id="alg5.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span> {type (2) in Equation <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.2 Selection of Basis ‣ 3 Method ‣ Accelerating Attention with Basis Decomposition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>}

<table id="A0.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}\;\leftarrow\;\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{C}\,\mathbf{B}\\
\mathbf{B}\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>𝐁</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}\;\leftarrow\;\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{C}\,\mathbf{B}\\
\mathbf{B}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg5.l2a" class="ltx_listingline">
          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
          
          
         Reconstructed matrix <math id="alg5.l2a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Almost Sure Full Rank of Random Matrices Theorem</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Almost Sure Full Rank of Random Matrices). ‣ 3.2 Selection of Basis ‣ 3 Method ‣ Accelerating Attention with Basis Decomposition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1. Define the polynomial map <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{W})=\det(\mathbf{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{W})=\det(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Let</p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p:\mathbb{R}^{r^{2}}\;\to\;\mathbb{R},\quad p(\mathbf{W})\;=\;\det(\mathbf{W})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msup><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p:\mathbb{R}^{r^{2}}\;\to\;\mathbb{R},\quad p(\mathbf{W})\;=\;\det(\mathbf{W}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is a polynomial (in <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> variables)
and it is not the zero polynomial, since, for instance,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\bigl(\mathbf{I}_{r}\bigr)\;=\;\det(\mathbf{I}_{r})\;=\;1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\bigl(\mathbf{I}_{r}\bigr)\;=\;\det(\mathbf{I}_{r})\;=\;1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{I}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{I}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\times r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\times r</annotation></semantics></math> identity matrix.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2. The zero set of a nontrivial polynomial has measure zero.
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Consider</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\;=\;\{\,x\in\mathbb{R}^{r^{2}}\mid p(x)=0\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\;=\;\{\,x\in\mathbb{R}^{r^{2}}\mid p(x)=0\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is a nontrivial real polynomial, its zero set <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is a real
algebraic variety of dimension <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;r^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;r^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence we know</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(Z)\;=\;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(Z)\;=\;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">(In simple terms, <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is a “lower-dimensional” subset of <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{r^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{r^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.)</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3. Absolute continuity of <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and conclusion.
<br class="ltx_break"></span>By hypothesis, the measure <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> (the distribution of <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math>) is absolutely
continuous with respect to the Lebesgue measure <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\ll\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\ll\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence for any Lebesgue null set <math id="A1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(A)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(A)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, <math id="A1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="A1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(Z)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(Z)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(Z)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(Z)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
But <math id="A1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> exactly corresponds to
the event <math id="A1.p4.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\det(\mathbf{W})=0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\det(\mathbf{W})=0\}</annotation></semantics></math> in the space of all matrix entries.
Therefore</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(\det(\mathbf{W})=0)\;=\;\mu(Z)\;=\;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\det(\mathbf{W})=0)\;=\;\mu(Z)\;=\;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">which implies <math id="A1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(\det(\mathbf{W})\neq 0)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\det(\mathbf{W})\neq 0)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(\mathrm{rank}(\mathbf{W})=r)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\mathrm{rank}(\mathbf{W})=r)=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>BD for VO in MHA</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we introduce the BD transformation for value and output projection matrices. The right part of Equation <a href="#S3.E10" title="In 3.4 BD for Multi-Head Attention ‣ 3 Method ‣ Accelerating Attention with Basis Decomposition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> can be converted to (using row &amp; first in Equation <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.2 Selection of Basis ‣ 3 Method ‣ Accelerating Attention with Basis Decomposition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>):</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{i}\mathbf{W}_{o}^{i}=\mathbf{X}(\mathbf{W}_{v}^{i}\mathbf{W}_{o}^{i})=\mathbf{X}(\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{I}\\
\mathbf{C}_{vo}^{i}\end{bmatrix}\mathbf{B}_{vo}^{i})=({\mathbf{X}_{:,\,1:d_{h}}}+\mathbf{X}_{:,\,d_{h}:d}\mathbf{C}_{vo}^{i})\mathbf{B}_{vo}^{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>𝐈</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐁</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐁</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{i}\mathbf{W}_{o}^{i}=\mathbf{X}(\mathbf{W}_{v}^{i}\mathbf{W}_{o}^{i})=\mathbf{X}(\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{I}\\
\mathbf{C}_{vo}^{i}\end{bmatrix}\mathbf{B}_{vo}^{i})=({\mathbf{X}_{:,\,1:d_{h}}}+\mathbf{X}_{:,\,d_{h}:d}\mathbf{C}_{vo}^{i})\mathbf{B}_{vo}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}_{vo}^{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{h}\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐁</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}_{vo}^{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{h}\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the first-<math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> row basis and <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}_{vo}^{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{(d-d_{h})\times d_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}_{vo}^{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{(d-d_{h})\times d_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> the coefficient matrix. Similar to Equation <a href="#S3.E12" title="In 3.4 BD for Multi-Head Attention ‣ 3 Method ‣ Accelerating Attention with Basis Decomposition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>, we can redefine value and output projection matrices to avoid calculating each head separately:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E14X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{V}^{\prime}={[\mathbf{X}_{:,\,1:d_{h}}]}^{\times n}+\mathbf{X}_{:,\,d_{h}:d}\mathbf{C}_{vo},\quad\text{where}\;\mathbf{C}_{vo}:=[\mathbf{C}_{vo}^{1},\dots,\mathbf{C}_{vo}^{n}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mi>𝐂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{V}^{\prime}={[\mathbf{X}_{:,\,1:d_{h}}]}^{\times n}+\mathbf{X}_{:,\,d_{h}:d}\mathbf{C}_{vo},\quad\text{where}\;\mathbf{C}_{vo}:=[\mathbf{C}_{vo}^{1},\dots,\mathbf{C}_{vo}^{n}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E14Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E14Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[\mathbf{V}_{1}^{\prime},\dots,\mathbf{V}_{n}^{\prime}]=\mathbf{V}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[\mathbf{V}_{1}^{\prime},\dots,\mathbf{V}_{n}^{\prime}]=\mathbf{V}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E14Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E14Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{O}_{i}^{\prime}=\text{softmax}(\frac{\mathbf{Q}_{i}^{\prime}{\mathbf{K}_{i}^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d_{h}}})\mathbf{V}_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐎</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{O}_{i}^{\prime}=\text{softmax}(\frac{\mathbf{Q}_{i}^{\prime}{\mathbf{K}_{i}^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d_{h}}})\mathbf{V}_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E14Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E14Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{Y}=[\mathbf{O}_{1}^{\prime},\dots,\mathbf{O}_{n}^{\prime}]\mathbf{B}_{vo},\quad\text{where}\;\mathbf{B}_{vo}:=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{B}_{vo}^{1}\\
\vdots\\
\mathbf{B}_{vo}^{n}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐎</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐎</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝐁</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝐁</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{Y}=[\mathbf{O}_{1}^{\prime},\dots,\mathbf{O}_{n}^{\prime}]\mathbf{B}_{vo},\quad\text{where}\;\mathbf{B}_{vo}:=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{B}_{vo}^{1}\\
\vdots\\
\mathbf{B}_{vo}^{n}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{[\mathbf{X}_{:,\,1:d_{h}}]}^{\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{[\mathbf{X}_{:,\,1:d_{h}}]}^{\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> means repeat matrix <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> times along second dimension. The <span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">last</span> version is similar.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Hyperparameters for BDA Training</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the IWSLT’14 English-to-German task, we followed the standard Transformer setup with the <span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Noam</span> learning-rate schedule <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaswani et al., 2017</a>)</cite>.
The embedding dimension was set to 512, with a feed-forward dimension of 2048.
We used a batch size of 10,240 tokens and trained for 20,000 steps.
Dropout was 0.1 and label smoothing was 0.1.
The model contained 6 layers with 4 attention heads.
For simplicity, we removed positional embeddings inside the MHA module but retained them in the embedding layer (the effect of positional embeddings on BD is discussed in Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Effect of Positional Embedding on BD ‣ Accelerating Attention with Basis Decomposition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>).
The learning rate scale was varied in <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0.5,1,2,4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0.5,1,2,4\}</annotation></semantics></math> (Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 BDA Training Evaluation ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Accelerating Attention with Basis Decomposition" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>).
Training employed the Adam optimizer with 6,000 warmup steps.
Beam search with a beam size of 2 was used for evaluation, and BLEU scores were reported using the checkpoint with the lowest validation perplexity.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">All hyperparameters for BDA were kept <span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">identical</span> to those of MHA to ensure a fair comparison.
Moreover, this also shows that BDA naturally matches the training dynamics of MHA, achieving comparable performance without any hyperparameter tuning.
As a result, existing LLM training pipelines can migrate from MHA to BDA at essentially no cost.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Effect of Positional Embedding on BD</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We briefly discuss how positional embeddings interact with Basis Decomposition (BD).</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Embedding-layer positional embedding.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Any positional embedding applied at the embedding layer (e.g., learned positional embeddings or sinusoidal embeddings added to input tokens) does not affect BD. Since BD only restructures the projection matrices inside the attention, the addition of position-dependent vectors at the input embedding layer is orthogonal to BD’s reformulation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">MHA-internal positional embedding.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When positional embeddings are applied inside the multi-head attention (MHA) module, the formulation changes. For example, vanilla Rotary Position Embedding (RoPE) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Su et al., 2021</a>)</cite> modifies the attention score computation as</p>
<table id="A4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{n}\mathbf{W}_{q}\,\mathbf{W}_{k}^{\top}\mathbf{X}_{m}^{\top}\quad\longrightarrow\quad\mathbf{X}_{n}\mathbf{W}_{q}\,\mathbf{R}_{n-m}\,\mathbf{W}_{k}^{\top}\mathbf{X}_{m}^{\top}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{n}\mathbf{W}_{q}\,\mathbf{W}_{k}^{\top}\mathbf{X}_{m}^{\top}\quad\longrightarrow\quad\mathbf{X}_{n}\mathbf{W}_{q}\,\mathbf{R}_{n-m}\,\mathbf{W}_{k}^{\top}\mathbf{X}_{m}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{n-m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{n-m}</annotation></semantics></math> is a rotation matrix depending on relative positions <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-m</annotation></semantics></math>.
BD guarantees the exact factorization</p>
<table id="A4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{q}\mathbf{W}_{k}^{\top}=\mathbf{B}[\mathbf{I},\mathbf{C}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{q}\mathbf{W}_{k}^{\top}=\mathbf{B}[\mathbf{I},\mathbf{C}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">but in general BD cannot guarantee</p>
<table id="A4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{q}\mathbf{R}_{n-m}\mathbf{W}_{k}^{\top}=\mathbf{B}\mathbf{R}_{n-m}[\mathbf{I},\mathbf{C}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐁𝐑</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐂</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{q}\mathbf{R}_{n-m}\mathbf{W}_{k}^{\top}=\mathbf{B}\mathbf{R}_{n-m}[\mathbf{I},\mathbf{C}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Thus, vanilla RoPE breaks the exactness of BD.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Decoupled RoPE as a solution.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DeepSeek proposes <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Decoupled RoPE</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>, which splits attention channels into RoPE and non-RoPE parts. BD can then be applied to the non-RoPE channels, while RoPE channels remain unchanged. This is also the strategy used in our experiments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Model-specific implications.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPT models</span> use positional embeddings only at the input embedding layer; thus BD is fully lossless for both QK and VO.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLaMA models</span> adopt vanilla RoPE inside MHA. Since RoPE is applied only to QK, BD remains lossless for VO projections but is not exact for QK.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DeepSeek models</span> employ Decoupled RoPE, which separates RoPE and non-RoPE channels in QK. BD can be applied losslessly to the non-RoPE channels of QK, and to all VO projections.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, the compatibility of BD with positional embeddings depends on how positional information is integrated. Embedding-layer positional encodings pose no issue, while RoPE inside MHA requires modifications (e.g., Decoupled RoPE).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>LLM Usage</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Large Language Models (LLMs) were used solely as a writing assistant to polish grammar.
They were not involved in research ideation, experiment design, analysis, or drafting of scientific content.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span><span id="A5.T4.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Numerical reconstruction errors of BD</span> for <math id="A5.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{q}\mathbf{W}_{k}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{q}\mathbf{W}_{k}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> (QK) and <math id="A5.T4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{v}\mathbf{W}_{o}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>o</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{v}\mathbf{W}_{o}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> (VO) under different floating-point formats.
Values are averaged across all heads and all layers of the DeepSeek-V2-Lite model.
We compare two strategies for selecting the BD basis: (i) always using the first <math id="A5.T4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> rows (<span id="A5.T4.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">First-<math id="A5.T4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math></span>), and (ii) choosing between the first or last <math id="A5.T4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> rows depending on which yields the smaller residual (<span id="A5.T4.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Residual-min</span>).
We report absolute mean squared error (MSE) and normalized mean squared error (NMSE).
The results confirm that BD introduces only <span id="A5.T4.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">negligible</span> perturbations to the matrix products, with <span id="A5.T4.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Residual-min</span> consistently outperforming <span id="A5.T4.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">First-<math id="A5.T4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math></span>, and improving error by at least one order of magnitude in FP32.</figcaption>
